@startuml sequence-resident-pickup
title Sequence Diagram(Resident Pickup Handover)
actor Resident
actor Staff
participant "Web UI" as UI
participant "Pickup API" as API
database "PostgreSQL" as SQL

Resident -> Staff : present the pickup code
Staff -> UI : enter the pickup code
UI -> API : POST /pickup/verify  (pickupCode)
API -> SQL : find the pickup code
alt code not found
  API --> UI : 404 Not Found
  UI -> Staff : reject the handover
else code expired or revoked
  API --> UI : 404 Not Found
  UI -> Staff : reject the handover and ask for a new code
else code valid
  API --> UI : 200 { parcelSummary, location }
  UI -> Staff : show the parcel and its location
  Staff -> Staff : fetch the parcel from the shelf
  Staff -> UI : confirm the handover
  UI -> API : POST /pickup/confirm  (pickupCode, result)
  API -> SQL : begin transaction, lock the pickup code
  alt code already used
    API -> SQL : no write, the handover already exists
    API --> UI : 200 Handover, the one already recorded
    UI -> Staff : show the handover already recorded
  else code still active
    API -> SQL : mark code used, insert handover, free location
    API --> UI : 200 Handover
    UI -> Staff : handover recorded
  end
end
note over API : operatorId is taken from the authenticated session (CR-007)
note over API, SQL : POST /pickup/confirm is idempotent by pickup code: a repeat returns the recorded handover with the same 200 and never writes a second row (NFR-4)
note over API : the contract folds expired and revoked codes into 404 "not found or invalid"
@enduml
